#!/bin/bash
# Install Ollie OS: the window behind the "Install Ollie OS" icon, like
# Batocera's "Install on a new disk". Pick the drive, confirm that it will be
# erased, watch the progress, restart. The work is done by ollie-install.
set -uo pipefail

readonly TITLE="Install Ollie OS"
readonly NEED_BYTES=$((25 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024 + 64 * 1024 * 1024))
log="$(mktemp /tmp/ollie-install.XXXXXX.log)"

gb() { awk -v b="$1" 'BEGIN {printf "%.0f GB", b / 1000000000}'; }

# The drive Ollie OS is running from is never offered.
live_disk=""
if src="$(findmnt -no SOURCE /run/archiso/bootmnt 2>/dev/null)" || src="$(cat /run/ollie-bootdev 2>/dev/null)"; then
    live_disk="$(lsblk -sno NAME,TYPE "$src" 2>/dev/null | awk '$2 == "disk" {gsub(/[^A-Za-z0-9]/, "", $1); print $1; exit}')"
fi

# What is on a drive now, in a few words.
contents() { # contents DISK
    local fs labels types
    fs="$(lsblk -nro FSTYPE "$1" | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ')"
    labels="$(lsblk -nro LABEL,PARTLABEL "$1" | tr '\n' ' ')"
    types="$(lsblk -nro PARTTYPE "$1" | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z' | tr '\n' ' ')"
    if [[ "$fs" == *apfs* || "$fs" == *hfsplus* || "$types" == *7c3457ef-0000-11aa-aa11-00306543ecac* ]]; then
        echo "has macOS on it"
    elif [[ "$fs" == *ntfs* || "$labels" == *"Microsoft"* ]]; then
        echo "has Windows on it"
    elif [[ "$labels" == *OLLIE* ]]; then
        echo "has Ollie OS on it"
    elif [[ "$fs" == *btrfs* || "$fs" == *ext4* ]]; then
        echo "has Linux on it"
    elif [[ -z "${fs// /}" ]]; then
        echo "empty"
    else
        echo "has files on it"
    fi
}
kind() { # kind DISK: internal or USB, and the connection
    local tran rm
    tran="$(lsblk -dno TRAN "$1" | tr -d ' ')" rm="$(lsblk -dno RM "$1" | tr -d ' ')"
    case "$tran" in
    usb) echo "USB drive" ;;
    nvme) echo "internal NVMe SSD" ;;
    sata | ata) [[ "$rm" == 1 ]] && echo "removable drive" || echo "internal drive" ;;
    mmc) echo "SD / eMMC" ;;
    *) echo "drive" ;;
    esac
}

kdialog --title "$TITLE" --yes-label "Choose a drive" --no-label "Cancel" --yesno \
    "Install Ollie OS onto a drive of this computer, so it starts without the USB.

Like Batocera's \"Install on a new disk\": the drive you pick is erased
completely and Ollie OS gets all of it.

The installed Ollie OS starts on new computers (Dells, Intel Macs, the Steam
Machine) and on older Dells set to Legacy / BIOS." || exit 0

# --- Which drive ------------------------------------------------------------------
items=() n=0
while read -r name type; do
    [[ "$type" == disk ]] || continue
    case "$name" in loop* | zram* | sr* | ram*) continue ;; esac
    [[ "$name" == "$live_disk" ]] && continue
    bytes="$(lsblk -bdno SIZE "/dev/$name")"
    ((bytes >= NEED_BYTES)) || continue
    model="$(lsblk -dno MODEL "/dev/$name" | xargs)"
    items+=("/dev/$name" "$(gb "$bytes")  $(kind "/dev/$name")  ${model:+$model  }($(contents "/dev/$name"))" off)
    n=$((n + 1))
done < <(lsblk -dnro NAME,TYPE)

if ((n == 0)); then
    kdialog --title "$TITLE" --sorry "No drive to install onto: none of 25 GB or more was found (the USB Ollie OS is running from is not counted).

On a Dell whose own drive does not show up: restart, press F2 at the Dell logo, and under
System Configuration > SATA Operation choose AHCI instead of RAID On. Windows on that drive
may stop starting after that change, so only do it if you are replacing it."
    exit 0
fi
disk="$(kdialog --title "$TITLE" --geometry 720x320 --radiolist "Install Ollie OS onto which drive? It will be erased." "${items[@]}")" || exit 0
[[ -n "$disk" ]] || { kdialog --title "$TITLE" --msgbox "Nothing was changed: no drive was picked."; exit 0; }

# --- Confirm ---------------------------------------------------------------------
what="$(contents "$disk")"
warn=""
case "$what" in
"has macOS on it") warn="This is a Mac drive with macOS on it: macOS and all its files will be gone. To get macOS back you would reinstall it from Apple's Internet Recovery (hold Option+Command+R at start-up)." ;;
"has Windows on it") warn="This drive has Windows on it: Windows and all its files will be gone." ;;
esac
details="$(lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,FSTYPE,LABEL "$disk" 2>/dev/null)"
choice="$(kdialog --title "$TITLE" --geometry 640x380 --checklist \
    "Everything on $disk ($(gb "$(lsblk -bdno SIZE "$disk")"), $(kind "$disk")) will be erased.
${warn:+
$warn
}
$details" \
    understood "I understand that everything on this drive will be erased" off)" || exit 0
[[ "$choice" == *understood* ]] || {
    kdialog --title "$TITLE" --msgbox "Nothing was changed: the box was not ticked."
    exit 0
}

# The time zone this Ollie OS already uses, or UTC.
tz="$(readlink /etc/localtime 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's|.*/zoneinfo/||p')"
[[ -n "$tz" ]] || tz=UTC

# --- Install ---------------------------------------------------------------------
bar="$(kdialog --title "$TITLE" --progressbar "Preparing the drive..." 100)"
qdbus6 $bar showCancelButton false >/dev/null 2>&1
OLLIE_INSTALL_DISK="$disk" OLLIE_INSTALL_YES=1 OLLIE_INSTALL_PROGRESS=1 OLLIE_INSTALL_TIMEZONE="$tz" \
    sudo -n --preserve-env=OLLIE_INSTALL_DISK,OLLIE_INSTALL_YES,OLLIE_INSTALL_PROGRESS,OLLIE_INSTALL_TIMEZONE \
    /usr/local/bin/ollie-install </dev/null 2>&1 | tee "$log" |
    while read -r word pct text; do
        [[ "$word" == PROGRESS ]] || continue
        qdbus6 $bar Set "" value "$pct" >/dev/null 2>&1
        qdbus6 $bar setLabelText "$text... ($pct%)" >/dev/null 2>&1
    done
rc=${PIPESTATUS[0]}
qdbus6 $bar close >/dev/null 2>&1

if ((rc != 0)) || ! grep -q '^PROGRESS 100 ' "$log"; then
    cp "$log" "$HOME/Desktop/Install-Ollie-OS-problem.txt" 2>/dev/null
    kdialog --title "$TITLE" --error "Installing did not finish:

$(sed 's/\x1b\[[0-9;]*m//g' "$log" | grep -iE 'error|failed|could not' | tail -n 3)

The details are on the desktop (Install-Ollie-OS-problem.txt). DC - Debug Computer can help find out more."
    exit 1
fi

if kdialog --title "$TITLE" --yes-label "Restart now" --no-label "Later" --yesno \
    "Ollie OS is installed on $disk.

Remove the USB drive, then restart. On its first start it asks you to create a
username and password.

If the computer still starts the old system:
  Dell: tap F12 at the Dell logo and pick the drive (\"UEFI: ...\" or \"OLLIE_BOOT\").
  Mac:  hold Option while it starts and pick \"EFI Boot\"."; then
    systemctl reboot
fi
